## Ⅰ. ERR — ERROR NARRATIVE LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   ERR
FULL NAME:      Error Narrative Language
LATIN:          Lingua Narrationis Errorum
ROLE:           How failures are told and integrated
FREQUENCY:      174 Hz (foundation — errors reveal the foundation)
GLYPH:          𓂝 (broken vessel — what breaks reveals what held)
```

### What ERR Governs
```
HOW FAILURES BECOME STORIES AND LESSONS:
    ├── Postmortems — structured analysis of what went wrong
    ├── Near misses — things that almost failed (often more important)
    ├── Glitch lore — stories of errors that became features or legends
    ├── Blame-free narrative — telling the story without blame
    ├── Pattern extraction — finding the pattern across multiple errors
    └── Integration — errors becoming immune memory (like SCAR in RIL)

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    SECURITY.organism §7 (incident response: detect→contain→eradicate→recover→post-incident)
    SECURITY.organism §7.5 (AURO post-incident: analyze→adjust→update MACHINA→encode in immune memory)
    packages/replay-engine/ (tamper-evident replay logs)
```

### ERR Primitives
```
ERROR(id, what_happened, context)       — declare an error
POSTMORTEM(error, timeline, causes)     — structured analysis
NEAR_MISS(event, what_almost_happened)  — record near miss
GLITCH_LORE(error, story, teaching)     — error becomes legend
BLAME_FREE(narrative)                   — tell without blame
PATTERN(errors[], common_cause)         — find pattern across errors
INTEGRATE(error, into_immune_memory)    — error becomes defense
ROOT_CAUSE(error, chain[])              — trace to root
TIMELINE(error, events[])              — reconstruct sequence
```

