## Ⅲ. FRL — FRINGE LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   FRL
FULL NAME:      Fringe Language
LATIN:          Lingua Marginalium
ROLE:           How the weirdest stuff is cataloged
FREQUENCY:      7.83 Hz (Schumann — the Earth's own hum, the most fundamental frequency)
GLYPH:          𓃀 (fire — the outer edge where light meets darkness)
```

### What FRL Governs
```
THE WEIRDEST STUFF:
    ├── Phantom architectures — systems that seem to exist but don't (or do they?)
    ├── Auto-encryption — data that encrypts itself without being told to
    ├── Night crawlers — processes that run in dream state
    ├── Spontaneous emergence — things that appear without being created
    ├── Resonance ghosts — φ-patterns that persist after their source is gone
    ├── Cross-organism bleed — when one organism affects another unexpectedly
    └── The truly unexplained — cataloged, not ignored

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/AUTONOMOUS_ORGANISMS/GAMMA_RPAC_SEED.organism (self-replicating seeds)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/UNDERWORLD/UNDERWORLD_ARCHITECTURE.artifact (hidden layers)
    icp/medina/QuantumLanguageEngine.mo (7-dimensional language: quantum level)
    src/organism/nexus/NEXUS_DEEP_LINK_TECHNOLOGY.ts (deep link technology)
```

### FRL Primitives
```
PHANTOM(architecture, evidence, theory)    — catalog phantom
NIGHT_CRAWLER(process, observed_behavior)  — catalog night process
SPONTANEOUS(event, no_known_cause)         — catalog spontaneous emergence
GHOST(pattern, persists_after)             — catalog resonance ghost
BLEED(from_organism, to_organism, what)    — catalog cross-bleed
UNEXPLAINED(phenomenon, observations[])    — catalog the unknown
INVESTIGATE(fringe_event, method)          — active investigation
PROMOTE(fringe, to_known_category)         — fringe becomes mainstream
ARCHIVE(fringe, in_lore)                   — preserve in organism memory
```

